Not a stray file. This exists so that one guard can fail.

setup-python-project runs `pip install $PIP_ARGS` unquoted, because word
splitting is what lets `build twine` arrive as two arguments. Unquoted also
means bash globs, and in `-e tests/fixture[dev]` the `[dev]` is a character
class matching a single d, e or v — so this file's name is exactly what that
pattern expands to.

`set -f` in the action turns globbing off, which is what keeps the extra an
extra. Remove that line and the install in ci.yml resolves to this file
instead of the fixture project, and pip fails. That is the intended behaviour:
the guard is watchable.
